---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="PCI DSS Compliance for AI: Protect Cardholder Data in LLM Prompts"
  description="Keep cardholder data out of AI APIs. AI Privacy Gateway auto-masks payment card numbers (with Luhn validation), bank accounts, and financial identifiers before they reach ChatGPT, Claude, and coding tools — reducing PCI DSS scope."
  keywords="PCI DSS AI合规,金融数据AI脱敏,银行卡号脱敏,支付数据保护AI,GLBA金融隐私AI"
  canonicalURL="https://privacygw.pages.dev/pci-dss-compliance"
  ogType="article"
  hreflang={[
    { lang: 'en', url: 'https://privacygw.pages.dev/pci-dss-compliance' },
    { lang: 'x-default', url: 'https://privacygw.pages.dev/pci-dss-compliance' },
  ]}>
  <Nav />

  <section class="seo-page">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="seo-header">
        <div class="seo-badge">Financial Compliance</div>
        <h1>PCI DSS Compliance for AI: Keep Cardholder Data Out of LLM Prompts</h1>
        <p class="seo-subtitle">
          Analysts, engineers, and support agents paste payment card numbers, bank accounts, and
          transaction data into ChatGPT, Claude, and coding tools every day. Each paste risks a PCI
          DSS violation and expands your compliance scope. AI Privacy Gateway masks cardholder data
          before it leaves your infrastructure.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="seo-tldr glass">
        <strong>TL;DR:</strong> Payment card numbers are masked locally (with Luhn validation) and
        replaced with placeholders before any AI API call. The AI provider never sees cardholder
        data, so masked traffic falls outside PCI DSS scope.
      </div>

      <h2>The PCI DSS Problem with AI Tools</h2>
      <div class="challenge-grid">
        <div class="challenge-card glass">
          <div class="challenge-num">1</div>
          <h3>Cardholder Data in Prompts</h3>
          <p>Debugging a payment failure means pasting card numbers and transaction logs into an AI assistant — a direct PCI DSS violation if unredacted.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="challenge-card glass">
          <div class="challenge-num">2</div>
          <h3>Scope Expansion</h3>
          <p>Any system that stores, processes, or transmits cardholder data is in scope. An AI API receiving raw PANs drags the provider into your PCI scope assessment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="challenge-card glass">
          <div class="challenge-num">3</div>
          <h3>Financial Privacy Laws</h3>
          <p>GLBA, CCPA, and state financial privacy laws restrict sharing financial data with third parties — including AI providers.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="challenge-card glass">
          <div class="challenge-num">4</div>
          <h3>Proprietary IP Leakage</h3>
          <p>Trading models, risk algorithms, and customer portfolios are competitive moats. Sending them to AI APIs for analysis exposes your IP.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>How AI Privacy Gateway Solves It</h2>
      <h3>Cardholder Data Masking with Luhn Validation</h3>
      <p>The gateway detects 16–19 digit card numbers and validates them with the Luhn algorithm
      before masking — reducing false positives on order IDs and account numbers. Bank accounts,
      amounts, and financial identifiers are also covered.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Payment card numbers (Luhn-validated) masked before egress</li>
        <li>Bank accounts, amounts, and transaction data covered</li>
        <li>Masked data falls outside PCI DSS cardholder-data scope</li>
        <li>Per-decision audit logs prove data minimization for assessors</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="diagram-flow glass">
        <div class="diagram-row">
          <div class="diagram-node">Analyst / Agent</div>
          <div class="diagram-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="diagram-node diagram-accent">Privacy Gateway<br/>(masks PAN locally)</div>
          <div class="diagram-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="diagram-node diagram-alt">AI API<br/>(sees placeholders)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="diagram-row-sub">
          <span class="diagram-check">&#10003; No cardholder data egress</span>
          <span class="diagram-check">&#10003; PCI scope reduced</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Deployment</h2>
      <div class="code-block glass">
        <div class="code-block-title">Docker</div>
        <pre><code>docker run -d --name ai-privacy-gw -p 9999:9999 \
  -v ./vault_data:/app/vault_data \
  ghcr.io/gunxueqiu6/ai-privacy-gateway:lite</code></pre>
      </div>
      <p>Point your AI clients to <code>http://localhost:9999/v1</code>. Masking, classification, and audit happen automatically.</p>

      <div class="seo-cta">
        <h2>Reduce PCI DSS Scope for AI Usage</h2>
        <p>Deploy in 30 seconds. No code changes. Audit-ready evidence included.</p>
        <div class="seo-cta-buttons">
          <a href="/download" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Get Started Free</a>
          <a href="/demo" class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg">Try the Demo</a>
          <a href="/pricing" class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg">Enterprise</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <script type="application/ld+json">{
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": [
          { "@type": "Question", "name": "Does masking card numbers remove PCI DSS obligations?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Masking removes cardholder data from AI traffic, reducing PCI scope, but full PCI compliance still requires your overall controls." } },
          { "@type": "Question", "name": "How is card detection accurate?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "16-19 digit numbers are validated with the Luhn algorithm before masking, reducing false positives." } },
          { "@type": "Question", "name": "Does it work on-premise?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Local deployment on bare metal, VM, Kubernetes, or Docker — data never leaves your network." } }
        ]
      }</script>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .seo-page { padding: 8rem 0 4rem; }
  .seo-page .container { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .seo-header { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .seo-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 0.35rem 0.85rem; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--primary); background: rgba(134, 239, 172, 0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(134, 239, 172, 0.15); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .seo-page h1 { font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .seo-subtitle { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.85; }
  .seo-tldr { padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .seo-tldr strong { color: var(--primary); }
  .seo-page h2 { font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin: 3rem 0 1rem; padding-bottom: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .seo-page h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem; }
  .seo-page p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.85; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .seo-page ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .seo-page ul li { padding: 0.5rem 0 0.5rem 1.5rem; position: relative; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }
  .seo-page ul li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.9rem; width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--primary); opacity: 0.5; }
  .seo-page a { color: var(--primary); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .seo-page code { background: var(--bg-deep); padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }
  .challenge-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .challenge-card { padding: 1.75rem; }
  .challenge-num { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--primary); opacity: 0.5; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; line-height: 1; }
  .challenge-card h3 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .challenge-card p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .diagram-flow { padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .diagram-row { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .diagram-row-sub { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .diagram-check { font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--primary); font-weight: 500; }
  .diagram-node { padding: 0.6rem 1.25rem; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 600; background: rgba(134, 239, 172, 0.06); border: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--primary); text-align: center; }
  .diagram-accent { color: var(--accent); background: rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.06); }
  .diagram-alt { color: var(--warning); background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.06); }
  .diagram-arrow { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .code-block { padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .code-block-title { font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
  .code-block pre { margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto; }
  .code-block code { color: var(--primary); }
  .seo-cta { text-align: center; padding: 3rem 2rem; background: var(--glass-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; margin-top: 3rem; }
  .seo-cta h2 { margin-top: 0; border: none; }
  .seo-cta p { color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .seo-cta-buttons { display: flex; gap: 1rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  @media (max-width: 768px) { .seo-page { padding: 6rem 0 3rem; } .seo-page h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; } .challenge-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .diagram-row { flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; } }
</style>
